# No Em-Dashes

Never use em-dashes (`—`, U+2014) or en-dashes (`–`, U+2013) in any output: chat responses, code, comments, commit messages, docs, or file names. Use a plain hyphen-minus (`-`, U+002D) instead.

- For a pause or aside, rewrite with a hyphen, comma, parentheses, or a new sentence.
- For ranges, use a hyphen: `1-10`, not `1–10`.
- Applies to generated text AND edited files. Do not introduce these characters even if nearby text already contains them.

## Examples

```
❌ The build failed — the tests were missing.
✅ The build failed - the tests were missing.
✅ The build failed. The tests were missing.

❌ pages 5–9
✅ pages 5-9
```
